# Copy to server/.env to change any of these. Everything is optional.

# Port OmniPilot runs on (open http://localhost:<PORT>).
PORT=8899
# OmniPilot only accepts connections from this computer.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# --- SDK access from other devices (Raspberry Pi, ESP32...; see docs/SDK.md) ---
# Both are needed: OmniPilot refuses to listen on the network without a token.
# The token only opens question-answering (/api/ask, /api/chat, MathPilot), never
# integrations, approvals or Watcher settings. Use 16+ random characters, e.g. from:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# OMNIPILOT_API_TOKEN=

# --- AI (Groq, free tier): required ---
# Get a key at https://console.groq.com/keys. Requests (and web pages agents read) are sent
# to Groq to be answered. Voice recordings are not: Whisper transcribes them on this computer.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# The main model (the strongest on Groq's free tier) and the ones used when it's rate-limited:
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# GROQ_FALLBACK_MODELS=qwen/qwen3.8-27b,openai/gpt-oss-20b
# How hard the main model thinks before answering: low, medium (default) or high.
# GROQ_REASONING=medium
# GROQ_TIMEOUT_MS=45000
# ROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
# Voice input: the local Whisper model (base, about 140 MB, downloads once into server/data/models)
# OMNIPILOT_WHISPER_MODEL=base

# Turn features off:
# ROUTER_MODE=heuristic   # keyword routing only, no model
# AGENT_LLM=off           # agents use only their built-in knowledge
# CODE_VERIFY=off         # never run code CodePilot writes
# MATHPILOT=off           # stop MathPilot's background identity search

# --- Optional: E2B cloud sandbox (https://e2b.dev) ---
# Lets CodePilot (and routines) run commands in a throwaway cloud machine: "run `python main.py` in my
# flashcard project", and project tests that need packages or the network. Only that project's files are
# uploaded; commands never run on your computer. Uses your E2B account (free tier available). Keep it secret.
# E2B_API_KEY=
# E2B=off                        # keep the key but turn it off

# --- Optional: Browser Use (https://browser-use.com) ---
# A cloud AI browser for jobs that need clicking through a site ("go to my school's website and find this
# week's lunch menu"). Read-only: it's told never to sign in, buy, post or send. Uses your Browser Use credits.
# BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=           # (BROWSERUSE_API_KEY works too)

# --- Optional: web tools (Browserbase, https://browserbase.com) ---
# Lets Helper search the web and read pages (read-only) for web-research questions.
# Queries and page addresses go to Browserbase; uses your Browserbase plan (free tier available).
# BROWSERBASE_API_KEY=
# WEB_TOOLS=off                  # keep the key but turn the tools off
# WEB_TOOLS_MAX_CALLS=10         # per agent attempt
# WEB_TOOLS_MAX_SESSIONS=1       # full browser sessions per agent attempt (always closed afterwards)
# WEB_TOOLS_DEADLINE_MS=90000    # overall time limit per agent attempt


# --- Hosting OmniPilot on a server (so it runs while your computer is off): see docs/DEPLOY.md ---
# OMNIPILOT_PASSWORD=            # 12+ characters; needed to sign in from anywhere but this computer
# OMNIPILOT_PUBLIC_URL=          # e.g. https://my-omnipilot.fly.dev
# TZ=America/New_York            # the clock routines run on (servers default to UTC)
# OMNIPILOT_CRON_SECRET=         # lets a scheduler (Cloudflare cron) wake OmniPilot to run routines
# GROQ_DAILY_TOKENS=200000       # your Groq daily allowance per model (for the usage warning)
# OMNIPILOT_AI_CACHE=off         # don't reuse answers to repeated questions

# --- Optional: tracing with Langfuse (https://langfuse.com) ---
# Every request becomes a trace with each AI call in it (prompt, answer, model, timing).
# Prompts and answers go to your Langfuse project.
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://us.cloud.langfuse.com   # your region (default: EU, https://cloud.langfuse.com)

# Keys can also go in .env in the project folder; server/.env wins if both set the same one.

# --- The AI model: local first (privacy), Groq only when needed ---
# OmniPilot answers with the model on this computer (Ollama) and uses Groq only for hard jobs (whole
# projects, 3D models, long research write-ups) or when the local answer isn't usable.
# Install: brew install ollama && ollama pull qwen3:4b-instruct   (2.5 GB)
# OMNIPILOT_LOCAL_MODEL=qwen3:4b-instruct

# --- Tool services (each optional; OmniPilot picks one per job and keeps a shared budget per request) ---
# Check them any time: cd engine && uv run python -m omnipilot_engine.tools.status verify
# EXA_API_KEY=            # web search (first choice)
# TAVILY_API_KEY=         # web search (backup)
# YDC_API_KEY=            # You.com web search (backup)
# TABSTACK_API_KEY=       # reading a page as clean text (first choice)
# APIFY_API_KEY=          # bulk scraping with Apify Actors (only when a request needs many pages)
# DAYTONA_API_KEY=        # code sandboxes (backup to E2B)
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=       # up-to-date library documentation for CodePilot
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=       # actions in 800+ apps you connect in Composio (changes need your approval)
# ARCADE_API_KEY=         # actions in apps through Arcade, tools like Gmail.ListEmails (changes need your approval)
# TRIGGER_API_KEY=        # Trigger.dev background jobs (TRIGGER_SECRET_KEY works too)
# SERPAPI_API_KEY=        # Google results (web search backup)
# MEM0_API_KEY=           # cloud memory (only when you ask OmniPilot to remember/recall something)
# ZEP_API_KEY=            # cloud memory (backup to Mem0)
# LLAMAINDEX_API_KEY=     # LlamaParse: PDFs, Word, slides and spreadsheets to text
# RESEND_API_KEY=         # sending email (every send needs your approval; needs a domain verified in Resend)
# QDRANT_API_KEY=         # Qdrant vector search over notes you ask OmniPilot to index
# QDRANT_ENDPOINT=        # your cluster URL, e.g. https://xyz.cloud.qdrant.io (embeddings: ollama pull nomic-embed-text)
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=       # speech to text fallback, only when on-device Whisper can't run
# OMNIPILOT_CLOUD_SPEECH=0  # never send recordings to Deepgram
# Stagehand (cloud browser) uses BROWSERBASE_API_KEY with your GROQ_API_KEY for its model.

# --- Infisical (optional): keys come from the project in .infisical.json before this file ---
# INFISICAL_TOKEN=           # a machine identity's token, for servers without `infisical login`
# OMNIPILOT_INFISICAL_ENV=dev  # which Infisical environment to read
# OMNIPILOT_INFISICAL=0      # don't read Infisical
